From 9490c61cfc7a63a7205914333f6fb1c39db9c15c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iasnezhkov <iasnezhkov@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:25:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2: MDP hardware MM21->NV12 converter with CPU fallback

Adds MdpImageConverter, a second ImageConverter implementation next to
LibyuvImageConverter (patch 4), driving the vendor libdpframework.so
DpBlitStream C++ API (DpEngine RDMA/WROT under the mdp_drv_mt6789
chardev, /dev/mtk_mdp) instead of the NEON detile loop. Measured cost
of the CPU path on this device: ~2.75 ms/1080p frame, ~4.9 ms/1440p
(task brief, 23.09); the vendor MDP path was independently proven
bit-exact MM21->NV12 on the device with tools/rigs/mdpconv.c this same
session (logs/o66_1-2309/mdp-path.txt).

libdpframework.so already has a real Soong module (vendor/ikko/mindone
Android.bp:7591, cc_prebuilt_library_shared, soc_specific: true) and
other vendor blobs in this tree (libgpu_aux) already list it as a
shared_lib - so this links it properly via v4l2/Android.bp shared_libs
instead of dlopen, avoiding the linker-namespace risk the research
notes flagged for a plain pushed executable.

That module lives in the vendor/ikko/mindone Soong namespace, which this
project namespace (root Android.bp, soong_namespace) did not import, so
Soong analysis failed for every target of the tree with "depends on
undefined module libdpframework". The root Android.bp now imports
vendor/ikko/mindone; nothing else in the project resolves differently
(of the 36 module names this project uses, only libdpframework is defined
in that namespace, and none of its own module names are).

No public header for
DpBlitStream exists anywhere in the checked-out tree (confirmed by
find), so MdpImageConverter.cpp redeclares the five methods and two
enums the IDA analysis already recovered (mangled names matched
exactly against libdpframework.so own dynamic symbol table) at file
scope, matching the real (unnamespaced) mangling. sizeof(DpBlitStream)
is unknown without the real header - same as mdpconv.c, this
constructs the object with placement new into a fixed 8192-byte
calloc-equivalent buffer rather than a real operator-new DpBlitStream
call, which would undersize the allocation against our own (empty)
class declaration. MdpImageConverter::Create() probes /dev/mtk_mdp
with a throwaway open() first so a sepolicy or DAC denial fails
cleanly (return nullptr) before any DpBlitStream object is
constructed.

Zero-copy: VideoFrame::detileFrom (VideoFrame.cpp) now takes a
primary and a fallback ImageConverter. For the primary, it reads the
destination C2GraphicBlock dmabuf fd and real plane layout
(offset/stride/size per plane) from the block native handle via
GraphicBufferMapper::getPlaneLayouts - the standard AOSP gralloc4
metadata query, which does not mmap the buffer - and never touches
pixel data itself. Only if the primary is absent or its
convertMM21ToNV12 call returns false does it fall back to the
existing mGraphicBlock map plus libyuv path. V4L2Decoder remembers a
first-failure flag, mMdpFailed, and logs the MDP to CPU fallback
exactly once per stream instead of every frame.

Two points the vendor blob has no header to confirm, flagged as
hypotheses for the first real device run (matching mdpconv.c own open
questions in mdp-path.txt):
 - setSrcBuffer/setDstBuffer take an unsigned int pointer, pitch,
   assumed to be per-plane byte SIZES (mdpconv.c proved this for a
   tightly packed, no-padding buffer); for a gralloc destination with
   real vstride padding, this patch passes the plane 1 argument as the
   real queried byte OFFSET of plane 1, under the hypothesis that
   DpBlitStream computes each successive plane address as the
   cumulative sum of the given plane sizes/offsets within the single
   fd (there is no separate offset parameter in the recovered API).
 - setSrcConfig/setDstConfig trailing DpRect pointer is passed
   nullptr for full frame, as mdpconv.c already does successfully on
   the device.

Both the source (TiledCaptureBuffer, patch 4) and the destination
(gralloc) side are always converted at the coded/aligned size, same as
the existing libyuv path (VideoFrame::detileFrom was already being
called with mCodedSize, not the cropped visible size) - so MDP is
never asked to scale, only reformat, avoiding a second, separate
open question about DpRect based cropping.

Sepolicy (device/ikko/mindone/sepolicy/vendor/mtk_hal_c2.te): the base
MediaTek policy (device/mediatek/sepolicy_vndr/base/vendor/
mtk_hal_c2.te) already grants
  allow mtk_hal_c2 mtk_mdp_device:chr_file r_file_perms;
  allow mtk_hal_c2 mtk_mdp_sync_device:chr_file r_file_perms;
covering /dev/mtk_mdp and /dev/mdp_sync (file_contexts line 321/323)
for the exact domain this v4l2-based Codec2 HAL already runs as (same
service, same domain as the stock mtk_hal_c2 it replaces) - no new
rule needed for those two nodes. strings on the pulled 64-bit
libdpframework.so additionally references /dev/sw_sync, not currently
granted to mtk_hal_c2 anywhere in this tree; added defensively below
since mdpconv.c synchronous invalidate() never exercised that code
path and it is unconfirmed whether our narrow
setSrc/setDstConfig+Buffer+invalidate call sequence ever reaches it.

